{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nu={\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Queuing the measurement for the gap just registered on the authority-transition question. The probe removes one node from a three-voter cluster, leaves it transport-reachable, and then sends TimeoutNow from that removed node to a surviving follower three times, waiting after each round for the cluster to settle and recording the leader and term. Local construction feedback shows leadership changing in all three rounds with the term advancing from three to five while a leader exists between rounds; an earlier wiring mistake that delivered the request back to the sender was found and corrected before this run, so the queued harness sends from the removed node's own transport. The retained receipt is what the gap answer will rest on.\\\",\n \\\"experiment\\\":{\n  \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"f59ffda2c1554082ae054646e92c2508f0a-question-0\\\",\n  \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_generated_test.go\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-timeoutnow\\\",\\\"s-requestvote\\\"],\n  \\\"scope\\\":{\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A three-voter in-memory cluster is started, one follower is removed through the public API and stays transport-reachable, and then three rounds follow: each round sends a TimeoutNow request from the removed node's own transport to a surviving follower that is not the current leader, waits for the leadership to change, and records how many rounds changed leadership, how many ended with a leader present, and the target's term after each round.\\\",\n   \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n    \\\"Cluster, transports and FSM are the repository's own MakeCluster, InmemTransport and MockFSM facilities; the removal uses RemoveServer.\\\",\n    \\\"The removed node keeps its transport routes, which is the situation of a server taken out of the configuration but not shut down.\\\",\n    \\\"Timers are shortened so each round settles quickly; the request is sent from the removed node's own transport, which already routes to every peer.\\\"\n   ]},\n  \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Bootstrap a three-voter cluster with shortened election, heartbeat and lease timers; wait for a leader and apply one command; choose a follower, RemoveServer it and wait until its own configuration no longer contains it; then for three rounds pick a surviving follower other than the current leader, record the current leader and the target's term, send TimeoutNow from the removed node's transport to the target, wait up to five seconds for the leadership to change, and count the rounds that changed leadership and the rounds that ended with a leader; finally emit the counts, whether churn persisted over at least two rounds and the term recorded after each round.\\\",\n  \\\"requirement\\\":\\\"A cluster must not let a server outside the configuration in force repeatedly displace its leader: leadership changes must not be triggerable round after round by the same non-member sender.\\\",\n  \\\"responsibility\\\":\\\"Raft itself: the TimeoutNow handler decides what a received transfer trigger means, and the vote handler decides how much trust to extend to a transfer-flagged campaign.\\\",\n  \\\"anchors\\\":[\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-timeoutnow\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"timeoutNow\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":2232,\\\"end_line\\\":2232},\n   {\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"s-requestvote\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"requestVote\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1626,\\\"end_line\\\":1626}\n  ]\n }\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
